    "summary": "A woman&#039;s hair ornament / head-band (?).  Made from a rectangular piece of red tabby woollen cloth decorated with white, red and green glass (?) beads, strung together to form diamond patterning (beadwork).  Black cotton woven cloth stitched to sides, with linen tow (?) (covered with red cloth as before), wrapped with woven cotton ribbon, hanging down on either side.  More red cloth on opposite side to beadwork, with large, roughly beaten metal disc, suspended with threaded cream glass (?) beads.  Paper label glued to object; printed Russian text, incomplete.",
